Monday Update
Trade Alert: Buy DKS and BBBY calls&nbsp;Dow rips higher while Nasdaq sinks=
 amid rising bond yieldsStocks are swirling in all directions today as tech=
s are hit by sharp gains in government bond yields while big cap value flou=
rishes.The Dow Jones Industrial Average jumped by 635.48 points, or 2%, to =
32,131.78. S&amp;P 500 was higher by 1% to 3,880.41. Nasdaq slumped by 0.4%=
 to 12,864.15. Technology was the steepest decliner while industrials and m=
aterials were among the biggest gainers after midday on Monday.The US 10-ye=
ar yields rose by 4.7 basis points to 1.61%, the highest level since Januar=
y 2020. The dollar index was up by 0.4% to 92.31, and gold fell by $19.8 pe=
r troy ounce to $1,679.February's employment report is the latest in a slew=
 of "solid" economic reports suggesting the US economy continues to recover=
 from the 2020 recession.Accelerating US economic growth has been the most =
significant driver of equity purchases by households during the past 30 yea=
rs, according to Goldman Sachs. Net equity buying by households has been gr=
eater than all the other major investor types when real yields and breakeve=
n inflation were rising, according to the firm.Goldman lifted its household=
 net equity demand outlook for this year to $350 billion from $100 billion =
and projects a doubling of corporate equity demand in 2021 relative to the =
previous year to $300 billion. It said inflows into equity mutual funds and=
 exchange-traded funds totaled $163 billion since the start of February, th=
e largest five-week inflow on record in absolute dollar terms.In company ne=
ws, Ross Stores (ROST) said it opened seven stores in five states in Februa=
ry and March as part of plans to add 40 Ross and 20 dd's DISCOUNTS location=
s during fiscal 2021. Shares jumped by 6% intraday.XpresSpa Group (XSPA), a=
 health and wellness company, said Monday it is collaborating with United A=
irlines (UAL) to open a testing facility at Houston's George Bush Intercont=
inental Airport. Shares of the airline rose 7.2%, the third-biggest perform=
er on S&amp;P 500.Portfolio: Our order for Microsoft did not fill Friday. W=
e now have two new ideas for you.*NEW RECOMMENDATIONDicks Sporting Goods (D=
KS) March 75 calls-- Symbol: DKS210319C00075000-- Order: Buy at $4.60 lmt d=
ay only-- If filled, set up to sell half at $6.00 lmt gtc and half at $7.85=
 lmt gtc-- If filled, set stop at $3.25 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*=
Bed, Bath and Beyond (BBBY) March 25 calls-- Symbol: BBBY210319C00025000-- =
Order: Buy at $5.40 lmt day only-- If filled, set up to sell half at $7.10 =
lmt gtc and half at $9.20 lmt gtc-- If filled, set stop at $3.80 stp, good =
after 10:30 a.m. ET only*Thanks for reading,Jon D. MarkmanAll recommendatio=
ns are for monthly options expiring on the third Friday of the specified mo=
nth unless otherwise noted. All stops are good after 10:30 a.m. Eastern onl=
